{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And the terafim</b> — like the shape of a pack-saddle, but the correct interpretation in my eyes is the camel's saddle-cushion, like \"send a kar to the ruler of the land\" (Isaiah 16:1) and similarly \"and in the karot\" (ibid. 66:20), and the custom of the kar or its rider is to call it the kari, and so Rachel took the terafim and placed them in the place where the camel's kar is:" "<b>And she sat upon them.</b> And she was not in the tent."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "Resolved וי\"מ בכר as 'and the terafim,' reading the lemma as the heading for the phrase וימצא בכר הגמל from verse 34."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:39.763750945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}